course: dictionary
lesson: 14418
title: Words that lie on top
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Overlying means lying on top of something else and covering it. Its clue is the prefix over-, which means above or on top. Overlie is built from over and lie, so one thing lies over another.
explain: «The overlying soil hid the old stones.» The soil lies on top of the stones and covers them. Ask yourself: what is on top here? The answer tells you what overlying means.
explain: Scientists use the word for rock. «The overlying layer of rock covers the layer below it.» Rocks form in layers, one on another, so the layer on top is the overlying one. In medicine, «the overlying skin» is the skin lying on top of a lump or a bone.
fact: Overlying means lying on top of something else and covering it.
fact: The prefix over- means above or on top, so overlying means lying over.
fact: In science and geography, the overlying layer is the one on top of a layer that lies deeper down.
fact: Overlying can also mean more noticeable or on the surface, over something deeper (a formal use).
fact: A quick check: swap in «lying on top of» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The overlying sand covered the buried shells.» What does overlying mean here? | *Lying on top and covering | Empty and hollow | Lying far underneath, out of sight | Shiny and bright like glass
exercise: In a cliff, «the overlying rock layer» is the one lying over the layer below. Which layer is on top? | The layer under the others | The sea beside the cliff | *The layer that covers the one below | The rocks lying at the bottom of the sea
exercise: Ella says overlying means under. Is she right? | No, it means sleepy | Yes, it means underneath | Yes, it means far away | *No, overlying means on top, not under
test: «The overlying skin on the bump was red and sore.» What does overlying mean here? | *Lying on top of the bump, covering it | Growing very quickly | Very old and cracked | Lying under the bump, out of sight
test: Scientists dig down and find: «The overlying layer is the newer one; the layer below it is older.» Which layer is older? | Neither can be dated | The overlying layer | Both are the same age | *The layer below
exam: «The overlying rock covered the sandy valley.» What does overlying mean? | Tall and thin | Lying beneath and hidden | Hot and dry | *Lying on top and covering
